{
  "_README": [
    "Not loaded by anything. Copy ONE of the two objects below into",
    ".claude/settings.local.json (not settings.json: the invocation is a fact about",
    "the machine, not about the project) and drop the leading underscore key.",
    "",
    "Which one: Claude Code runs a hook command through $SHELL -c when SHELL is set,",
    "otherwise %COMSPEC% /d /s /c on Windows, otherwise /bin/sh -c. Started from",
    "PowerShell, cmd or a shortcut, SHELL is unset and _windows applies. Started from",
    "Git Bash or WSL, SHELL is set and _posix applies -- on Windows too.",
    "",
    "Both call a script FILE rather than inlining an echo. That is deliberate: an",
    "inline command carrying JSON has to survive the shell's quoting, and cmd.exe",
    "keeps the double quotes that sh strips. A path to a script carries no quotes to",
    "get wrong.",
    "",
    "The command is relative to the project directory. If the hook never fires, an",
    "absolute path is the first thing to try.",
    "",
    "UNVERIFIED until you test it on this machine: add the block, run /clear, and see",
    "whether STATE.md comes back. Nothing appears means the hook is not firing -- a",
    "malformed hook is ignored silently, it does not report an error."
  ],

  "_windows": {
    "hooks": {
      "SessionStart": [
        {
          "hooks": [
            {
              "type": "command",
              "command": "powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .claude\\hooks\\session-start.ps1"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  },

  "_posix": {
    "hooks": {
      "SessionStart": [
        {
          "hooks": [
            {
              "type": "command",
              "command": "bash .claude/hooks/session-start.sh"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
